---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import {
  CodeBlockCanvas,
  CodeBlockChatResponse,
  CodeBlockFileExplorer,
  CodeBlockPlainText,
  CodeBlockPlayground,
  CodeBlockVariants,
  CodeBlockWebhook,
  CodeBlockWorkflowStep,
} from '../../components/CodeBlockDemo';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
---

<Docs
  title="Code Block"
  description="Shows code or text with a filename, line numbers, syntax colors, and a copy button, inline in a reply or filling a file pane."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Code Block</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    Shows code from a reply, a canvas, a workflow step, or a file. It colors every language Shiki knows, over 240, picks
    the language from the file name, and copies the exact source with one button.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8">
    <CodeBlockPlayground client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="A code step in a workflow review"
      code={`import { CodeBlock } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/code-block";

<CodeBlock
  code={step.source}
  language="python"
  filename="score_lead.py"
/>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>language</code> takes a name, an alias, or an extension, such as
      <code>typescript</code>, <code>ts</code>, or <code>py</code>, so a Markdown fence name can go straight in. Leave
      it out and the language comes from <code>filename</code>: <code>main.rs</code>,<code>Dockerfile</code>, and{' '}
      <code>.env.local</code> all work.
      <code>text</code>, <code>txt</code>, and unknown names show plain text. The header shows <code>filename</code>, or
      the language’s name.
      <code>lineNumbers</code> is on by default. <code>wrap</code> wraps long lines for prose such as notes, and hides
      line numbers.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Syntax colors</h2>
    <p>
      Shiki tokenizes the code with its JavaScript regex engine, so there is no WebAssembly and no inline styles. Each
      grammar loads the first time a block needs it, and the block shows plain text until then. Markdown also loads the
      languages of its fences. Code over 200,000 characters stays plain so a huge file can’t freeze the page.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="css"
      title="Recolor tokens for one theme"
      code={`[data-theme="sunset"] {
  --sprout-syntax-keyword: #c2410c;
  --sprout-syntax-string: #15803d;
  --sprout-syntax-comment: #78716c;
}`}
    />
    <p>
      Tokens get the classes <code>sprout-syntax-keyword</code>,<code>-string</code>, <code>-constant</code>,{' '}
      <code>-function</code>,<code>-parameter</code>, <code>-comment</code>, <code>-punctuation</code>,
      <code>-link</code>, and, for Markdown and diffs, <code>-heading</code>,<code>-inserted</code>, and{' '}
      <code>-deleted</code>. Each reads a matching
      <code>--sprout-syntax-*</code> variable and falls back to the theme’s info, success, warning, danger, and muted
      colors, so every theme works without setup.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Highlighted on the server"
      code={`import { preloadCodeLanguages } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/code-block";

await preloadCodeLanguages("tsx", "python");`}
    />
    <p>
      Await <code>preloadCodeLanguages</code> before server rendering to send colored HTML.{' '}
      <code>languageForFilename</code>,<code>codeLanguageName</code>, and <code>isHighlightedLanguage</code>
      expose the same lookup the block uses.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Variants</h2>
    <p>
      <code>inline</code> is a bordered card that scrolls after 24rem.
      <code>file</code> has no frame and fills its parent, so give the parent a height.
      <code>preview</code> drops the header and copy button and fades out at its parent’s height, for hover cards and
      thumbnails.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-6">
      <CodeBlockVariants client:load />
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">In a chat reply</h2>
    <p>
      Render fenced code from Markdown with the fence language and no filename. A fence without a language shows as{' '}
      <code>text</code>.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="A Markdown pre override"
      code={`pre({ node, children }) {
  const code = node?.children[0];
  if (code?.type !== "element" || code.tagName !== "code") return <pre>{children}</pre>;
  const language = languageClass(code)?.slice("language-".length) ?? "text";
  return <CodeBlock code={textOf(code).replace(/\\n$/, "")} language={language} />;
}`}
    />
    <div class="mt-6">
      <CodeBlockChatResponse client:load />
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Canvas and workflow steps</h2>
    <div class="mt-6 code-demo-recipes">
      <CodeBlockCanvas client:load />
      <CodeBlockWorkflowStep client:load />
      <CodeBlockPlainText client:load />
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">File pane</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="A file that changes"
      code={`<div className="flex h-full min-h-0 flex-col">
  <CodeBlock
    key={\`\${file.revision}:\${file.path}\`}
    code={file.content}
    filename={file.path}
    variant="file"
  />
  {file.content === "" && <p>This file is empty.</p>}
</div>`}
    />
    <p>
      A new <code>key</code> per file and revision resets the copy state and scroll position. Long paths truncate in the
      header; the region and the copy button still use the full path.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-6">
      <CodeBlockFileExplorer client:load />
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Shell examples</h2>
    <p>Turn off line numbers for shell commands so a copied command runs as is.</p>
    <div class="mt-6">
      <CodeBlockWebhook client:load />
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The code scrolls in a focusable region named after the file, or “<em>Language</em> code”, such as “TypeScript
      code”. The preview variant is not focusable. Line numbers are hidden from screen readers. The copy button is named
      “Copy <em>filename</em>” or “Copy code”, stays focusable while it copies, shows Copied for 2 seconds, and
      announces “Code copied to clipboard.” When the clipboard is blocked an alert says to select the code instead, and
      Copy tries again. On touch screens the button is 44px tall. The error fades in over 180ms, or appears at once with
      reduced motion.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
